==English==

===Etymology===
{{back-form|intrusion|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnˈtruːsɪv/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-intrusive.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|in|tru|sive|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Tending or apt to [[intrude]]; doing that which is not [[welcome]]; [[interrupting]] or [[disturbing]]; [[enter]]ing without [[right]] or [[welcome]].
#: ''Did it ever cross your mind that he might find all those questions you ask '''intrusive'''?''
# {{lb|en|geology}} Of rocks: forced, while in a [[plastic]] or molten state, into the cavities or between the cracks or layers of other rocks.

